  "body": "## What changed\n\nUpdate the 12 existing guide pages for the features listed in #2854.\nExplain the three file compatibility barriers beside their workflows.\nDescribe the current DXF generation refusal and the stored plasma recipe limits.\nExplain the tool shape window, checked preview, Deburr controls and Finish gap links.\nAdd linked models, LinuxCNC, post paths, viewport input, panel setups, startup files and Report instructions.\nKeep the AI connection pointer short. Issue #1949 owns the full AI guide.\nRecord the decisions in docs/decisions/2854-guide-refresh.md.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe merged features had no complete guide instructions.\nSome existing text described old behavior.\nRead the feature PR bodies and their merged code and tests:\n#2149, #2134, #2092, #2764, #2096, #2681, #2688, #2687, #1713,\n#2563, #2310, #2352, #2662, #2665, #2542, #1798 and #2122.\nProtection reached main through #2704.\nThe current Report buttons copy a screenshot automatically.\nThe older PR body described a separate copy button.\nIssues #2717, #2747 and #2741 need no user guide text, as #2854 states.\n\n## Tests\n\nRun `python3 -B -m unittest discover -s site/tests -p test_guide_refresh.py`.\nAll 12 GuideRefresh tests fail against unchanged upstream guide pages.\nAll 12 tests pass with this change.\n\nThe pins cover:\n\n- test_protection_explains_file_compatibility\n- test_dxf_placement_has_setup_and_operation_guidance\n- test_holder_reference_and_separate_editor_are_documented\n- test_plasma_recipes_name_material_and_thickness\n- test_deburr_filters_and_unreachable_edges_are_documented\n- test_finish_gap_links_are_documented\n- test_linked_model_source_changes_are_documented\n- test_linuxcnc_machine_and_post_are_documented\n- test_post_dialog_explains_script_location\n- test_viewport_input_and_saved_panel_layouts_are_documented\n- test_startup_paths_are_documented_for_cli_and_first_run\n- test_report_workflow_explains_clipboard_and_github\n\nMutation checks restore each guide page from upstream/main separately.\nEach restored page makes the pin fail. Each fixed page makes the pin pass again.\nAll 12 page mutations pass this red/green check:\n\n- automate/cli.md\n- check-and-post/machines.md\n- check-and-post/posting.md\n- getting-started/first-run.md\n- getting-started/keyboard-and-mouse.md\n- getting-started/workflows.md\n- operations/operations-2d.md\n- operations/operations-3d.md\n- operations/operations-plasma.md\n- reference/troubleshooting.md\n- set-up/setups.md\n- set-up/tools.md\n\nZola 0.23.6 `zola build` passes: 47 pages, 10 sections and no orphan pages.\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passes.\nThe gate selects no Rust tests because no Rust crate changed.\nClippy does not apply: no Rust crate changed.\n`git diff --check` passes.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The diff for `.nc` and `.cl` files is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo runtime CAM, GUI or controller tests run for this documentation change.\nNo screenshots or generated evidence enter the branch.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nPR #2799 touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\nFor these guide files, the overlap concerns different sections:\nmachines.md, setups.md, first-run.md and operations-plasma.md.\nPR #2799 changes mill-turn wording. This change adds other workflows.\nNo stack is needed.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #2854\n",
